    {
      "id": 192134,
      "name": "Bigbywolfe",
      "username": "Bigbywolfe",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/dbc845/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-03-17T01:21:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why would they just casually glance over Omnitron X getting destroyed in the Tactics timeline without explaining how that ever happened? You’d think that would be a really big deal for the heros and especially Unity after, you know, the whole Omnitron-U storyline, so why was this just ignored? Little bits like this kinda get lost in the fold</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Omnitron-X was already destroyed prior to Obliveaon so it was Omnitron-U that was lost I believe.<br>\nIt didn’t feel ignored to me at all.  The way I understood it, Heroic Omnitron survived Obliveaon in the RPG timeline and evil Omnitron is “dead”, seemingly for good. Heroic Omnitron didn’t survive Obliveaon in the Tactics timeline (much like Rook City) and evil Omnitron resurfaced.<br>\nUnless I completely misunderstood what they said he didn’t die during the Tactics timeline so much as never make it there at all.</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:18:50.773Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
